# appearance.schema — which layer may decide each key of the `appearance`
# subsystem (Hub -> Appearance -> Settings: per-user overrides that beat the
# active theme).
#
# Read by /usr/lib/w/w-conf-lib.sh during the load pass; see w-conf.md.
#
# Both keys are `user`: they tint only the logged-in user's own session (their
# rendered Hyprland config), so there is no root domain to protect — same
# reasoning as nightlight.schema. No vendor .conf ships for this subsystem: the
# unset default ("follow the active theme") is a plain fallback in the reader
# code, exactly like w-power's per-user idle keys.
#
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>       scope: system | user | both

# "" (unset) = follow the active theme's effects.conf/motion.conf. "off" =
# forced off regardless of theme. Bar position is NOT here — it already has a
# dedicated override slot in config/bar.json (see w-appearance).
BLUR	user
MOTION	user
